      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "6956bb06a8595f498400a4e1",
          "question": "<p>According to Bohr's theory the radius of electron in an orbit described by principal quantum number \\( n \\) and atomic number \\( Z \\) is proportional to</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>&nbsp;\\( Z^{2} n^{2} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{Z^{2}}{n^{2}} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{Z^{2}}{n} \\).</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{n^{2}}{Z} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "6956bb06a8595f498400a4ea",
          "question": "<p>The ratio of speed of an electron in ground state in&nbsp;Bohrs first orbit of hydrogen atom to velocity of light&nbsp;in air is</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>&nbsp;\\( \\frac{e^{2}}{2 \\varepsilon_{0} h c} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{2 e^{2} \\varepsilon_{0}}{h c} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{e^{3}}{2 \\varepsilon_{0} h c} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{2 \\varepsilon_{0} h c}{e^{2}} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "6956bb06a8595f498400a4ed",
          "question": "<p>How may different wavelengths may be observed in the&nbsp;spectrum from a hydrogen sample if the atoms are&nbsp;excited to states with principal quantum number \\( \\mathrm{n} \\) ?</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>&nbsp;\\( \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( n^{2} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{n^{2}+1}{2} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{n(n-1)}{2} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "6956bb06a8595f498400a500",
          "question": "<p>In Bohr model of hydrogen atom, the ratio of periods&nbsp;of revolution of an electron in \\( n=2 \\) and \\( n=1 \\) orbits is</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>2:1</p>",
            "<p>4:1</p>",
            "<p>8:1</p>",
            "<p>16:1</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "6956bb06a8595f498400a4f8",
          "question": "<p>Which one of the series of hydrogen spectrum is in&nbsp;the visible region</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>Lyman series</p>",
            "<p>Balmer series</p>",
            "<p>Paschen series</p>",
            "<p>Bracket series</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "6956bb06a8595f498400a510",
          "question": "<p>If the wavelength of the first line of the Balmer series&nbsp;of hydrogen is \\( 6561 A \\), the wavelength of the second&nbsp;line of the series should be</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13122</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mover><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></mover></math></p>",
            "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3280</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mover><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></mover></math></p>",
            "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4860</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mover><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></mover></math></p>",
            "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2187</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mover><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></mover></math></p>"
          ],
          "correct": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "6956bb06a8595f498400a513",
          "question": "<p>Which of the following is true</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>Lyman series is a continuous spectrum</p>",
            "<p>Paschen series is a line spectrum in the infrared</p>",
            "<p>Balmer series is a line spectrum in the ultraviolet</p>",
            "<p>The spectral series formula can be derived from the Rutherford model of the hydrogen atom</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "<p>Paschen series is a line spectrum in the infrared</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "6956bb06a8595f498400a4f0",
          "question": "<p>An electron changes its position from orbit \\( n=4 \\) to the orbit \\( n=2 \\) of an atom. The wavelength of the emitted radiations is ( \\( R= \\) Rydberg's constant)</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>&nbsp;\\( \\frac{16}{R} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{16}{3 R} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{16}{5 R} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{16}{7 R} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "<p>(1/&lambda;) = <em>R</em>((1/<em>n</em><sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup>) &ndash; (1/<em>n</em><sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>)) and <em>n</em><sub>1</sub> &lt; <em>n</em><sub>2</sub></p>\n<p>(1/&lambda;) = <em>R</em>((1/2<sup>2</sup>) &ndash; (1/4<sup>2</sup>))</p>\n<p>(1/&lambda;) = <em>R</em>(3/16)</p>\n<p>&lambda; = (16/3<em>R</em>)</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "6956bb06a8595f498400a50d",
          "question": "<p>The wavelength of the first line in Balmer series in the hydrogen spectrum is \\( \\lambda \\). What is the wavelength of&nbsp;the second line</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>&nbsp;\\( \\frac{20 \\lambda}{27} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{3 \\lambda}{16} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{5 \\lambda}{36} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{3 \\lambda}{4} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "6956bb06a8595f498400a505",
          "question": "<p>The ratio of the frequencies of the long wavelength&nbsp;limits of Lyman and Balmer series of hydrogen&nbsp;spectrum is</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>&nbsp;\\( 27: 5 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 5: 27 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 4: 1 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 1: 4 \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "6956bb06a8595f498400a547",
          "question": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In a hydrogen spectrum, &lambda; be the wavelength of first transition line of Lyman series. The wavelength difference will be \"a&lambda;\" between the wavelength of 3<sup>rd</sup> transition line of Paschen series and that of 2<sup>nd</sup> transition line of Balmer Series where a = _______.</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [],
          "correct": 0,
          "explanation": "5"
        },
        {
          "id": "6956bb06a8595f498400a541",
          "question": "<p>The momentum of an electron revolving in <em>n</em><sup>th</sup> orbit is given by: (Symbols have their usual meanings)</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
